-- title:
--   Ordinarity at odd p of a Uₚ-unit point with irreducible ordinary reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $N \geq 1$, and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers containing $p$ and every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology and with finite residue field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ outside $S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ outside $S$, to $\mathcal{O}'$. Assume $p \mid N$ and that $\chi$ extends to a homomorphism $\chi'$ on the corresponding algebra for $S \setminus \{p\}$ (via the inclusion of $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebras) with $\chi'(U_p) = u_p$ a unit. Let $\rho$ consist of a free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank two with an adically continuous action of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, i.e. for each $n$ some finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ has all its pointwise stabilising $\sigma$ satisfying $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}^n V$. Assume: the residual representation $\mathcal{O}'/\mathfrak{m} \otimes V$ stays irreducible over an algebraic closure of the residue field; the residual representation, regarded as an adic representation over the residue field, is ordinary at $p$; and for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Then $\rho$ is ordinary at $p$: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ having $p$ as a nonunit there is a submodule $L \subseteq V$ spanned by the first vector of some $\mathcal{O}'$-basis of $V$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\ 2$, stable under the decomposition group of $P$, and with $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in L$ for all $v \in V$ and all $\sigma$ in the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$.
--
--   This is the ordinarity at $p$ of the $p$-adic representation cut out by a weight-two eigenform point of level divisible by $p$ whose $U_p$-eigenvalue is a unit, in the form of Wiles' Theorem 2.1.4, under the extra hypotheses that $p$ is odd and that the residual representation is already absolutely irreducible and ordinary at $p$; nothing is asserted about $p = 2$, or about points with reducible or non-ordinary reduction, and no representation is constructed. It feeds the assembly of Hecke–Galois representation data in [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_isOrdinaryAt_of_primeFactors_subset`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_isOrdinaryAt_of_primeFactors_subset).
